# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# §15 Security headers, applied at the Cloudflare edge.
#
# IMPORTANT — why CSP is path-scoped instead of on `/*`:
# Cloudflare Workers static-assets `_headers` APPENDS headers from every matching
# rule (it does not let a more-specific rule override a less-specific one), and
# Modify-Response-Header Transform Rules do NOT apply to static-asset responses.
# So a strict CSP on `/*` plus a relaxed CSP on `/admin/*` produced TWO CSP
# headers on /admin — browsers enforce the intersection, which re-blocked the
# CMS. The only reliable fix is to ensure each path matches exactly ONE CSP rule:
#   - the strict marketing CSP is enumerated per top-level HTML route
#   - `/admin/*` carries its own relaxed CSP (CMS loads from a CDN + talks to
#     GitHub and the OAuth relay)
# Non-CSP security headers stay on `/*` (identical everywhere, no conflict).
# Marketing CSP posture is still zero-third-party, `script-src 'self'`.
#
# WHY THE MARKETING LIST IS ENUMERATED AND DUPLICATED:
# the default locale (en-au) is UNPREFIXED, so marketing pages live at top-level
# paths (`/pricing`, `/knowledge/…`) rather than under one `/en-au/*` that a
# single rule could cover. `_headers` has no way to say "everything except
# /admin", so each marketing route gets its own rule carrying a BYTE-IDENTICAL
# CSP. Adding a page under src/pages/[...locale]/ means adding a line here —
# and `npm run build` enforces exactly that: scripts/prepare-sites-output.mjs
# fails the build if a built HTML route matches zero or two CSP rules, or if the
# marketing CSP values have drifted apart. Don't hand-tune one line in isolation.
#
# NOTE: this file is currently INERT on the Sites host serving lumii.com.au —
# production responses carry none of these headers today. See public/_redirects
# for the same caveat and the evidence. The posture below is correct and ready
# for the day the project moves to a host that honours `_headers`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), browsing-topics=()
  # same-origin-allow-popups (not same-origin): the CMS at /admin opens a
  # cross-origin OAuth popup and needs window.opener to deliver the token back.
  # COOP same-origin severs window.opener for cross-origin popups → login aborts.
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# Strict marketing CSP — one rule per HTML route so /admin never inherits it.
/
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://scqxaziehzyekohhiuip.supabase.co https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.ingest.us.sentry.io https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
